{"claim_id": "S4-01", "task_id": "P5-1", "claim": "SUPERSEDED BY DIRECT EVIDENCE (round R2). Conjecture 4.1 EXISTS. The V_quad companion was retrieved from Zenodo (concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20455089) and placed in sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/refs/. Three versions exist. In v1.0 (version DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20455090, 10 pp) and v1.1 (10.5281/zenodo.20480603, 12 pp) the object numbered 4.1 is a THEOREM; in v1.2 (10.5281/zenodo.20481592, 12 pp) it is CONJECTURE 4.1, 'Painleve V (D5^(1)) classification'. The operator's hypothesis is therefore CONFIRMED exactly. The earlier finding arose because the repo's own bibitem{Vquad} cites version DOI 20455090 = v1.0, and because no copy of the companion was in the repo at all; the search that produced the finding covered the PERIOD-REP paper, a different document. Both the original claim and the R1 amendment are withdrawn. Finding S4-F1 is CLOSED.", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "REPORT.md", "output_hash": "43ece880af3f657a711a3ac768244915232cdeb0ec04b032925c20b028b4cf92", "label": "INSPECTED", "audit_r1": "AUDIT R1: CLAIM SCOPE CORRECTED; the original wording overstated the finding. The search actually covered sessions/2026-06-15/VQUAD-PERIODREP-PAPER-001, which is the PERIOD-REP paper, NOT the V_quad companion. The companion is a DISTINCT document, cited as bibitem{Vquad} ('The V_quad polynomial continued fraction: a Painleve-V standalone closure on the Sakai surface D5^(1)', Zenodo, version DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20455090), and a repo-wide search finds it ONLY as bibliography title strings -- no copy of the companion exists in this repo at ANY version. Therefore 'Conjecture 4.1 does not exist' is RETRACTED as a citation defect and restated as: the companion paper is absent from the repo, so Conjecture 4.1 can be neither confirmed nor refuted here. The operator's v1.0/v1.1 hypothesis is NOT confirmed either -- there is no copy to inspect.", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2", "label_before_r2": "STRUCTURAL", "audit_r2": "Relabelled INSPECTED under operator ruling 1(a): established by direct inspection of named files at commit 08aa0e2381b3dc37ee54a3200b7272755ca11d59; valid only for that commit.", "claim_before_r2": "No 'Conjecture 4.1' exists in the V_quad companion materials. Searching all of sessions/2026-06-15/VQUAD-PERIODREP-PAPER-001 returns only Fresan-Jossen Conjecture 1.3.2 and the descriptively-referenced 'master conjecture of the Sakai-stratification program' part (ii)(a) in section-7.md; section 4 is 'The main identity and its normalisation' and contains a theorem, not a conjecture. The D5^(1) attribution rests on VQ-N1/verdict.md (2026-05-29) and section-7.md. Finding S4-F1: operator must supply the correct pointer."}
{"claim_id": "S4-02", "task_id": "P5-1", "claim": "The D5^(1) conjecture is NOT about the f(z)=Sum Q_n z^n ODE. Per section-2.md L54-57 and rmk:provenance, L_phi is 'the scalar (Schroedinger) reduction of the V_quad Painleve-V linear problem' and annihilates phi(z)=Sum a_n z^n, the Riccati/WKB series seeded by sigma=-1/sqrt3 -- a different series from the PCF numerator generating function. Both systems were therefore analysed, as P5 step 1 directs.", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "REPORT.md", "output_hash": "43ece880af3f657a711a3ac768244915232cdeb0ec04b032925c20b028b4cf92", "label": "INSPECTED", "label_before_r2": "STRUCTURAL", "audit_r2": "Relabelled INSPECTED under operator ruling 1(a): established by direct inspection of named files at commit 08aa0e2381b3dc37ee54a3200b7272755ca11d59; valid only for that commit.", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2"}
{"claim_id": "S4-03", "task_id": "P5-2", "claim": "System A derived and certified: f(z)=Sum Q_n z^n for b(n)=3n^2+n+1 satisfies 3z^3 f'' + 10 z^2 f' + (z^2+5z-1) f = -1. The residual against the exact integer sequence Q=1,5,76,2361,125209,10144290,... vanishes identically at every order z^0..z^38 in exact arithmetic. Falsifier F2 did not fire.", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "formal_type.py", "output_hash": "12c53f529f490a512eb8d1cdf4fe11df8fa36fb6e27a8e1a5fdd51879cc1ec2f", "label": "PROVEN", "audit_r1": "AUDIT R1: label PROVEN UPHELD, with the basis restated. The proof is the SYMBOLIC derivation [1 - z*b(theta+1) - z^2] f = 1 with theta = z d/dz, which is exact and holds at all orders. The vanishing residual at z^0..z^38 against the exact integer sequence is CORROBORATION, not the proof; a finite check alone would not warrant PROVEN.", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2"}
{"claim_id": "S4-04", "task_id": "P5-2", "claim": "System B transcription certified two independent ways: (a) the paper's factorisation q2 = 4(2sqrt3-3) z^2 (z^2+z+3) expands exactly to the listed q2; (b) recomputing r = a^2/4 + a'/2 - b from (q0,q1,q2) reproduces the paper's printed r(z) = (11z^4+4z^2+4z+12)/(4 z^4 (z^2+z+3)^2) exactly. This validates the transcription and independently confirms the paper's eq:r. Falsifier F1 did not fire.", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "formal_type.py", "output_hash": "12c53f529f490a512eb8d1cdf4fe11df8fa36fb6e27a8e1a5fdd51879cc1ec2f", "label": "PROVEN", "audit_r1": "AUDIT R1: label PROVEN UPHELD. Two exact CAS identity verifications of a transcription; exact arithmetic, no tolerance.", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2"}
{"claim_id": "S4-05", "task_id": "P5-2", "claim": "System A formal type (exact, from normal form r_A = (-3z^2-5z+3)/(9z^3)): at z=0 the pole order is 3 (odd) => irregular RAMIFIED, ramification index 2, Katz invariant 1/2, exponential parts exp(-+(2/sqrt3) z^(-1/2)); z=0 is the only finite singular point; at z=infinity the pole order is 3 => irregular RAMIFIED, Katz invariant 1/2. Confirms the P5 premise that Channel Theory has a slope-1/2 ramified edge at z=0. Calibration: in u=sqrt(z) the actions are +-2/sqrt3, matching c=+2/sqrt(3) hard-coded in CC-PIPELINE-G2/g2_pade_borel.py.", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "formal_type.json", "output_hash": "c49cf8a547f60b66d201f48205ab83e6f5ec702eb14f628e8df0b7b4a19fed83", "label": "PROVEN", "audit_r1": "AUDIT R1: label PROVEN UPHELD, with a dependency named. The pole orders are computed in exact arithmetic (integers, no tolerance). The step from pole order to {ramified, Katz invariant} uses the STANDARD classification of second-order formal singularities, which is cited, not proved in session.", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2"}
{"claim_id": "S4-06", "task_id": "P5-2", "claim": "System B formal type (exact): at z=0 pole order 4 (even) => irregular UNRAMIFIED, Poincare rank 1, Katz invariant 1, exponential parts exp(-+(1/sqrt3)/z); at rho_pm = (-1 +- i sqrt11)/2 pole order 2 => regular singular; at z=infinity pole order 2 => regular singular. Every entry independently reproduces the paper's own prose in section-2.md L78-84 and tab:config. Confirms the P5 premise that the D5^(1) object is unramified.", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "formal_type.json", "output_hash": "c49cf8a547f60b66d201f48205ab83e6f5ec702eb14f628e8df0b7b4a19fed83", "label": "PROVEN", "audit_r1": "AUDIT R1: label PROVEN UPHELD. Same basis and same cited classification dependency as S4-05.", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2"}
{"claim_id": "S4-07", "task_id": "P5-2", "claim": "Action differences, obtained from the ODEs alone with no convention to interpret: System A in u=sqrt(z) has single action 2/sqrt3 = xi_0 and action DIFFERENCE 4/sqrt3 = zeta*; System B in z has single action 1/sqrt3 and action difference 2/sqrt3 = xi_0. This independently confirms P1's classification (b) that zeta* = 2 xi_0 is an action difference, not a change of variables. It also shows the Borel singularity sits at the action difference in both systems, consistent with L_V's exact factor p4 proportional to xi (xi + 2/sqrt3).", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "formal_type.json", "output_hash": "c49cf8a547f60b66d201f48205ab83e6f5ec702eb14f628e8df0b7b4a19fed83", "label": "PROVEN", "audit_r1": "AUDIT R1: label PROVEN UPHELD. Action values read off the exact normal forms; exact arithmetic.", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2"}
{"claim_id": "S4-08", "task_id": "P5-3", "claim": "SUPERSEDED (round R2). At the time of CT-S4, P5 step 3 was correctly HALTED because NOT FOUND in the repository, by filename and full-text search, was any rank-2 Painleve classification table. That halt was correct under the rules then in force. The operator has since supplied van der Put & Saito, Ann. Inst. Fourier 59 (2009) no. 7, 2611-2667, DOI 10.5802/aif.2502; the citation was verified and a copy placed at sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/refs/vanderPut-Saito-AIF-2009-59-7-2611.pdf (sha256 1666bd6be824a99fc0b48adbe48233a9b2a520fd7e8adf187e98d22525473605). Table 2.1, p. 2635, is extracted in CLASSIFICATION-TABLE.md. The halt condition is LIFTED.", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "PREREG.md", "output_hash": "6721fcae308938b16aa395cc5e55b5f920e58a024b532f0e8023f4434727e566", "label": "INSPECTED", "label_before_r2": "STRUCTURAL", "audit_r2": "Relabelled INSPECTED under operator ruling 1(a): established by direct inspection of named files at commit 08aa0e2381b3dc37ee54a3200b7272755ca11d59; valid only for that commit.", "claim_before_r2": "Step 3 HALTED and NOT executed, as P5 itself mandates: no Ohyama-Kawamuko-Sakai-Okamoto-type classification table of rank-2 linear systems exists in this repository (CT-S0-INVENTORY/REPORT.md section 3 item 7). VQ-N1 cites Sakai 2001, KNY 2017, Jimbo 1982, Okamoto 1987 but reproduces no table and records 'Okamoto 1987 pages PENDING'. No table was reconstructed from memory anywhere in this session.", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2"}
{"claim_id": "S4-09", "task_id": "P5-4", "claim": "VERDICT (c) INCONCLUSIVE. Within a fixed base coordinate the formal types are incompatible (Katz 1/2 ramified vs Katz 1 unramified), and no gauge or unramified change of variable can reconcile them. However the ramified double cover pi: w -> z = w^2 (equivalently Channel Theory's own uniformiser u = sqrt z) doubles the Katz invariant, sending System A's 1/2 to 1, exactly System B's value, with ramification index dropping 2 -> 1. So the slope-1/2 edge alone does NOT refute the D5^(1) attribution; it shows the two z-coordinates differ by a square. Verdict (a) is unavailable because step 3 could not run and the global singular configurations visibly differ (System A: one finite singular point, infinity ramified irregular; System B: three regular singular points plus one unramified irregular). Verdict (b) is unavailable because naming compatible Painleve types requires the missing table.", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "formal_type.json", "output_hash": "c49cf8a547f60b66d201f48205ab83e6f5ec702eb14f628e8df0b7b4a19fed83", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2"}
{"claim_id": "S4-10", "task_id": "P5-1", "claim": "Finding S4-F2: VQ-N1/verdict.md and the period-rep paper describe the linear system in INVERTED coordinates. VQ-N1: z=0 ordinary with exponents {0,1} and no z^(1/2) ramification, finite apparent Fuchsian points at (-1 +- i sqrt11)/6, infinity rank-1 unramified irregular with sigma_pm = +-1/sqrt3. L_phi: z=0 irregular Poincare rank 1 with exponential parts +-1/sqrt3, finite regular singular points at (-1 +- i sqrt11)/2, infinity regular singular. The finite points differ by a factor 3 (benign rescaling) but 0 and infinity are exchanged. Plausibly related by z -> 1/z, since VQ-N1's sigma_pm at infinity equals L_phi's exponential coefficients at 0, but this was NOT verified; VQ-N1's system is not written down in any readable file.", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "REPORT.md", "output_hash": "43ece880af3f657a711a3ac768244915232cdeb0ec04b032925c20b028b4cf92", "label": "INSPECTED", "label_before_r2": "STRUCTURAL", "audit_r2": "Relabelled INSPECTED under operator ruling 1(a): established by direct inspection of named files at commit 08aa0e2381b3dc37ee54a3200b7272755ca11d59; valid only for that commit.", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2"}
